@startuml
skinparam handwritten false
skinparam monochrome true
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam boxPadding 10

box "Hardware Layer" #LightGray
participant "Network Interface\n(Ethernet/Wi-Fi)" as Net
participant "DMA Controller" as DMA
end box

box "STM32 MCU Core" #White
participant "Interrupt Controller\n(NVIC / ISR)" as ISR
participant "MicroShield\n(C Library)" as Shield
participant "Main Superloop\n(while(1))" as Loop
database "Static RAM Buffer" as RAM
end box

== SCENARIO A: Superloop Failure Pattern (Anti-Pattern) ==
Net -> DMA : Flood of malicious frames (DoS Attack)
activate DMA
DMA -> RAM : Continuous silent background write
DMA -> RAM : Continuous silent background write
note over RAM #FFCCCC: Buffer Overflow Condition!\nUnprocessed data overwritten
Loop -> Loop : Execute slow application logic (e.g., I2C Sensor Read)
Loop -> RAM : Read buffer to evaluate threat (Too Late!)
note right: CPU starvation occurs;\nMain application freezes
deactivate DMA

== SCENARIO B: Proactive ISR-Level Interception (MicroShield Blueprint) ==
Net -> DMA : Deposit incoming frame (e.g., 128 bytes)
activate DMA
DMA -> RAM : Write single frame to bounded slot
DMA -> ISR : Assert Hardware Interrupt Request (IRQ)
deactivate DMA
activate ISR
ISR -> Loop : Suspend CPU execution context
Loop --[hidden]> ISR

ISR -> Shield : microshield_classify()
activate Shield
note over Shield: Deterministic O(d) execution\nNested execution paths
Shield --> ISR : Return: THREAT (1)
deactivate Shield

ISR -> DMA : Force Instant Hardware Pointer Reset
note over RAM: Frame dropped and memory\nslipped before ingestion
ISR -> Loop : Restore CPU context
deactivate ISR
Loop -> Loop : Resume application cycles (Zero impact)
@enduml

